      "content_body": "When Subscription Manager experiences timeouts or delivery failures, check if the relevant vendor status page reports an active incident. If the vendor is stable, investigate for expired API keys or clock synchronization issues that may prevent successful handshakes. Credential rotation that has not propagated to all service endpoints is a frequent cause of intermittent 'third-party API unavailable' errors. Escalate to engineering if the issue persists after configuration changes, or engage the vendor directly if the root cause is upstream service degradation. Applying a workaround, such as queuing requests locally, may be necessary during extended vendor outages."
